.TH CLOG_INFO 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
clog_info \- emit a log line at INFO level
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/clogger.h>

clog_info(clog lg, const char *fmt, ...);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Writes a log line at CLOG_INFO level and picks up __FILE__, __LINE__
and __func__ for you.  It appends no backtrace.

For a production service, INFO is the minimum level we recommend as the
default.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
lg     Logger handle (clog).
fmt    printf-style format string.
\&...    Format arguments (optional).
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
clog_info(lg, "server started on port %d", port);
clog_info(lg, "request handled in %ldms", elapsed_ms);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR clog_trace (3),
.BR clog_debug (3),
.BR clog_warn (3),
.BR clog_error (3),
.BR clog_alert (3),
.BR clog_fatal (3)
